  "id": "F1",
  "title": "After a rollback, the previous release can deliver a resolution-only head as completed findings work",
  "file": "src/pipeline/engine.ts",
  "A": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "A review round on a conflicting PR is partway through resolving the conflict when a deploy rolls back to the previous release. The older engine sees what looks like an ordinary conflict-resolution round, finishes it, pushes only the merge commit and marks the round succeeded, so the review findings are never implemented and nobody is told.",
   "reproduction": "unreproduced: this needs the base-release engine to resume a run state written by the head engine. I did not build a two-engine harness. The evidence below traces the old resume path through the base code.",
   "evidence": "At head, a conflict in mergeReviewBase (engine.ts:681-687) saves `conflictFiles` and `reviewResolution = {}` and returns null, with no needsHumanReason. buildLoop (engine.ts:899-918) then calls mergeForDelivery, which sets `conflictRound = round`, `pendingRebaseSha`, `preRebaseHead = reviewedSha`, `phase = \"loop\"` and `run.baseSha = tip`, and runs oneRound for the resolution. `reviewResolution.sha` is written only at the end ('review-resolution-complete'). The base engine has no `reviewResolution` field, so it ignores it. Its only early refusal is `if (ctx.state.needsHumanReason) throw`, and that field is unset here. On resume the phase is 'loop', so prepare does not run again. Base buildLoop computes `maxRounds = conflictRound + 1` and runs oneRound as a resolution round (`resolution = conflictRound === round`), then calls setPhase('deliver'). Base deliver, under `if (ctx.state.conflictRound !== undefined)`, runs validateMerge(preRebaseHead, run.baseSha), which passes because the merge commit's parents are reviewedSha and tip. It skips commitAll and pushes the merge as a successful round. Nothing in that path implements the findings. The later commit adds REVIEW_RESOLUTION_BLOCK to needsHumanReason while resolution is pending, precisely so the old engine's `if (needsHumanReason) throw` refuses the run."
  },
  "B": {
