    "command": "bun test \"$TMPDIR/adjudicate-617-9dkajfjt/adjudication.test.ts\" --test-name-pattern 'adjudication F1'",
    "output": "F1 saved {\"interrupted\":\"running\",\"reviewResolution\":{},\"conflictRound\":1,\"implementedRound\":1,\"lastReview\":\"approve\",\"cachedReview\":true,\"implementationCalls\":1,\"remoteUnchanged\":true}\nF1 rollback {\"resumed\":\"succeeded\",\"error\":null,\"implementationCalls\":1,\"remoteChanged\":true,\"findingsFileExists\":false,\"comments\":0}\n(pass) adjudication F1 rollback before resolution SHA"
   },
   "evidence": "The throwaway test interrupts HEAD immediately before recordVerified saves, after resolution gates, audit and approving review are cached, then resumes using the engine source extracted from the base commit; its runtime dependencies are unchanged between base and head. HEAD calls `await oneRound(ctx, ctx.state.round, null)` before setting `ctx.state.reviewResolution.sha = sha` and clearing conflictRound. During that interval, persisted implementedRound equals conflictRound and no needsHumanReason blocks the old engine. Base buildLoop has no reviewResolution handling: `const passed = await oneRound(ctx, round, holdout); if (passed) { await ctx.setPhase(\"deliver\"); return; }`. Its quick-profile path accepts the cached checks. The reproduction confirms delivery without a second implementation call or the findings file."
  }
