    "output": "Head-only throwaway restart probes passed at pending resolution, after durable implementation-ready, after the merge commit, after gates, and after review. Each resumed with status \"succeeded\", exactly two implementation calls in total, and zero comments."
   },
   "evidence": "HEAD parameterizes only `test.each([\"resolution\", \"findings\"] as const)`. Its fault points are `c.checkpoint === \"review-resolution-complete\"` and `c.round === 2` after implementation. Although the first fault fires before ctx.save writes, engine.ts:916 has already persisted reviewResolution.sha through updateRun. Both cases therefore require `if (!merge) throw new Error(\"missing resolution checkpoint\")` and never exercise pending reviewResolution. Base has no review-base resolution feature or corresponding restart cases. The coverage omission is real independently of F1, but it does not establish that HEAD mishandles those boundaries."
